# =====================================================================
# CLEAN FULL-GMLC PSAP ROUTING / GEOGRAPHIC CROSSCHECK v3
# =====================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# Find geographically abnormal PSAP routing across the ENTIRE:
#
#     e911_lte_master_gmlc.csv
#
#
# ACTUAL ID MODEL
# ---------------
#
# GMLC:
#     PSAP_ID
#     FCC_PSAP_ID
#
# Final_Join.tab:
#     NENA_ID
#     FCC_ID
#
#
# PRIMARY ROUTED-BOUNDARY MATCH:
#
#     canonical(GMLC.PSAP_ID)
#             ==
#     canonical(Boundary.NENA_ID)
#
# CONFIRMATION:
#
#     canonical(GMLC.FCC_PSAP_ID)
#             ==
#     canonical(Boundary.FCC_ID)
#
#
# Example:
#
#     GMLC.PSAP_ID       21980004
#     Boundary.NENA_ID   021980004
#
# canonical form:
#
#     21980004 == 21980004
#
#
# IMPORTANT
# ---------
# - GMLC.NENA_ID is NOT used. It does not exist.
# - Boundary.PSAP_ID is NOT required.
# - Names NEVER choose a polygon.
# - Names are QA/reporting only.
# - CSSNG_DATA_ADDITION is NOT used.
#
#
# EXPECTED PSAP
# -------------
# Caller coordinate
#       -> GeoPandas spatial join
#       -> Boundary NENA_ID / FCC_ID / names
#
# Cell coordinate
#       -> GeoPandas spatial join
#       -> Boundary NENA_ID / FCC_ID / names
#
#
# OUTPUT DISTANCES
# ----------------
# All distances are METERS:
#
#     Caller -> routed PSAP boundary
#     Caller -> expected PSAP boundary
#
#     Cell -> routed PSAP boundary
#     Cell -> expected PSAP boundary
#
#     Caller <-> Cell
#
#
# FILTERS
# -------
# Example:
#
#     MIN_CALLER_OUTSIDE_ROUTED_M = 19000
#
# means:
#
#     Caller must be at least 19 km OUTSIDE the routed PSAP.
#
# Set Caller/Cell min/max values to None to disable that filter.
#
#
# CLEAN MAIN OUTPUT
# -----------------
# psap_clean_full_gmlc_routing_v3.csv
#
# =====================================================================


